From 878e881b9ebddbc08905905b8cb287dba4de8fad Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: EscapeA <escapea@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 11:30:19 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(web): make theme styles table-driven and add neon,
 aurora, blueprint
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Promotes the theme system from four hand-wired styles to a table-driven one and
adds three new looks beside an upgraded `tech`:

- tech (upgraded): deep-space HUD — near-black navy, cyan accent, 128px/32px
  grid and a cyan wash down from the top.
- neon: near-black canvas, cyan/magenta pair, 3px scanlines plus neon card edges.
- aurora: deep indigo with three drifting aurora lights behind frosted cards.
- blueprint: light-first drafting grid — the first light tech look, so it ships
  both a `.blueprint` and a `.dark.blueprint` palette.

`styles/theme-style.ts` is now the single source (style list, `<html>` class
table, brightness lock, label keys, status-bar colour and picker swatch), so
`main.ts` and `useTheme.ts` no longer carry an `if` per style and
`getThemeOverrides` reads a `STYLE_PALETTES` registry instead of a ternary
chain. Material that colour variables cannot express — ambient background,
glass, glows — moves into the new `styles/style-layers.scss`.

The ambient layer has to sit above the cards. This is a floating-card layout,
so a page-background texture is covered by the cards and measures as flat
colour (verified by spectral analysis of a card screenshot). Hence a fixed
`body::after` at z-index 3 — above `.app-layout`, below naive-ui teleports so
menus stay clean — combined with translucent `--bg-main-surface` /
`--bg-sidebar-surface`; both halves are required for the texture to read.

All 11 locales get the new style labels.
